// endpoint_subscribe_github_workflow_run.proto — SubscribeGithubWorkflowRun:
// tell one workspace's agent, ONCE, when a GitHub Actions workflow run
// finishes. AGENT API section.
//
// DELIVERY. The one notice is submitted to the subscriber's session as a
// deferred prompt of origin
// conversation.v1.PromptOrigin.PROMPT_ORIGIN_GITHUB_WORKFLOW_RUN_NOTICE: it
// waits behind a running turn, wakes an idle agent, and the feed draws no row
// for it. It names the workflow, the run's conclusion, the head commit and
// the run's web address. No other notice is ever sent for the run, except
// the one sentence every GitHub subscription is owed when GitHub rejects
// agent-repl's credentials.
//
// A RUN ALREADY FINISHED is answered `already_completed`, and its notice is
// delivered at once: no subscription is held.
//
// SCOPE AND LIFETIME. A subscriber holds at most one subscription per run;
// subscribing again is an answer (`already_subscribed`). A subscription ends
// with the run's completion, when the subscriber unsubscribes, or when it
// closes however it closes. It is DURABLE across a daemon restart and a
// handover.

